v1.7.1 (2026-10-03):
           v1.7.0 + a security fix for roaming through a HUB (OCPI 2.2.1): every
           request from a hub connection must name the party behind the hub that sends it
           (OCPI-from-country-code / -party-id, one the hub announced through HubClientInfo
           in the module's role), and is scoped to that party's own sessions, charge
           records, tokens, reservations, charging profiles and command results. Before,
           one eMSP (or CPO) behind a hub could read or act on another's through the same
           connection. Results to a hub are addressed to the party that asked. Peer
           (non-hub) connections are unchanged. No migrations, no new settings: a drop-in
           upgrade from v1.7.0. Who is affected: RELEASE-NOTES-v1.7.1.md.

